From: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: RK816 battery and charger, and the board that
 needs it

/sys/class/power_supply/battery does not exist on an RK816 board under
mainline: the rk816s[] cell list in drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c has a pinctrl, a
clkout, a regulator, a pwrkey and an rtc cell, and no charger, so nothing ever
claims the fuel gauge. This adds the cell and the driver behind it, together
with the binding and the board device tree the TAQ-102 needs to use them.

The RK816 has a real coulomb counter, a battery voltage and current ADC, a
charge state machine and a VBUS presence bit. What it does not have is a state
of charge register. RK816_SOC_REG at 0xe0 is the first of the battery-backed
general purpose data registers - mainline's own rk808.h already names the block
RK816_DATA_REG(x) - and in five thousand lines of vendor driver it is written
in exactly one place, rk816_bat_save_dsoc() at rk816_battery.c:1438, with the
driver's own computed percentage, and read in exactly one, at :1445, on the
next boot. It is a scratch byte.

So the percentage here is the integral, not a lookup. The 32 bit coulomb
counter is preloaded once at probe from the relaxed open circuit voltage
through the battery's ocv-capacity table, divided by the full charge capacity
on every poll, and re-anchored in exactly one place: when the charger reports
termination, which is the only moment the true charge is known. Nothing is ever
derived from the loaded terminal voltage, which is what stops the percentage
swinging when a GPU load steps - the appliance on this board is a single GL
application, and a battery indicator that moves with the frame rate is worse
than none.

The vendor's software layer on top of the counter is not reproduced, and each
omission is marked at its site in the driver: the zero algorithm that bends the
last few percent onto the power-off voltage, FCC relearning, the current ADC
offset self-calibration, and the sleep discharge estimate. The consequence
worth stating up front is that this driver's 0 % is not the vendor's 0 %: the
system should shut down on voltage, not on capacity.

Three other things fall out of the hardware and are worth naming:

  - The volatile register range for the RK816 began at RK816_GASCNT_REG(0),
    which is 0xbb - 0, the *low* byte of the coulomb counter. Under
    REGCACHE_MAPLE that froze the counter's three high bytes, the relax
    voltages and currents, the ADC offset calibration and the power off minute
    counter at their first post-boot value. A gauge reading a 32 bit
    accumulator through that cache reads the same number for ever, silently.
    The range now covers the whole hardware updated block, 0xb8..0xdf.

  - The part cannot tell a wall adapter from a USB port. USB_EXIST and USB_EFF
    exist in the vendor header but are never read for presence; their only
    occurrences are two case labels in a switch on SUP_STS bits 6:4, which
    those bits cannot match. Presence is PLUG_IN_STS in RK808_VB_MON_REG, and
    the SDP/CDP/DCP split comes from the SoC USB PHY through extcon, exactly as
    the vendor's usb_in/ac_in do. Without extcon every charger is a 450 mA
    port and "ac" stays offline: slow, but honest.

  - The three supplies are named "battery", "usb" and "ac" rather than
    rk817-charger's "rk817-battery" and "rk817-charger". Those three names
    under /sys/class/power_supply are the userspace ABI on this class of board.

Every register offset, bit position, scaling constant, table and default was
read out of the Rockchip 4.4 vendor tree, and every number in the board's
battery node was converted from the vendor board file's own hexadecimal. None
of it has been run on hardware yet.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/rockchip,rk816.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/rockchip,rk816.yaml
@@ -78,6 +78,14 @@
     description:
       The input supply for otg-switch.
 
+  extcon:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to an extcon device, usually the SoC USB PHY, that performs
+      BC1.2 charger detection. The RK816 can tell that VBUS is present but
+      not what is supplying it, so without this every charger is treated as
+      a 450 mA USB port.
+
   regulators:
     type: object
     patternProperties:
@@ -87,6 +95,52 @@
         unevaluatedProperties: false
     additionalProperties: false
 
+  charger:
+    type: object
+    $ref: /schemas/power/supply/power-supply.yaml
+
+    properties:
+      monitored-battery:
+        description: |
+          A phandle to a monitored battery node that carries a valid value
+          for charge-full-design-microamp-hours,
+          charge-term-current-microamp,
+          constant-charge-current-max-microamp,
+          constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt,
+          voltage-max-design-microvolt, voltage-min-design-microvolt,
+          and a valid ocv-capacity table.
+
+      rockchip,resistor-sense-micro-ohms:
+        description:
+          Value in microohms of the battery sense resistor. The gauge's ADC
+          scaling constants are defined for 20 mOhm; the driver corrects for
+          the other supported value.
+        enum: [10000, 20000]
+
+      rockchip,sleep-enter-current-microamp:
+        description:
+          Value in microamps of the sleep enter current, which sets the
+          relax mode entry and exit thresholds.
+
+      rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp:
+        description:
+          Value in microamps of the sleep filter current, which sets the
+          sleep sample current.
+
+      input-current-limit-microamp:
+        description:
+          Maximum current the board may draw from a dedicated charging
+          port. Standard and charging downstream ports are held to their
+          BC1.2 values instead.
+
+    required:
+      - monitored-battery
+      - rockchip,resistor-sense-micro-ohms
+      - rockchip,sleep-enter-current-microamp
+      - rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp
+
+    additionalProperties: false
+
 patternProperties:
   '-pins$':
     type: object
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3126-taq102.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3126-taq102.dts
@@ -96,3 +96,115 @@
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The RK816 PMIC and the battery behind it.
+ *
+ * These two headers are re-included here rather than at the top of the file
+ * so that this is one self-contained block; both carry include guards, so a
+ * second include costs nothing.
+ */
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/rockchip.h>
+
+/*
+ * The PMIC sits on i2c2 at 0x1a, beside the GSL3673 touch controller at 0x40
+ * on the same bus; i2c0 is enabled with no children at all on this board.
+ * Its interrupt is GPIO0_A2, active low.
+ * Checked against the decompiled vendor DTB, where the same node reads
+ * interrupts = <0x02 0x08>.
+ *
+ * The regulators are deliberately not described. Nothing here needs them,
+ * and transcribing a rail constraint wrong is how a board stops booting;
+ * the vendor's DCDC and LDO constraints are a separate change with its own
+ * risk. "rockchip,system-power-controller" is left off for the same reason:
+ * it changes what happens on poweroff.
+ */
+&i2c2 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	pmic@1a {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rk816";
+		reg = <0x1a>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio0>;
+		interrupts = <RK_PA2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pmic_int_l>;
+		#clock-cells = <1>;
+		clock-output-names = "xin32k", "rk816-clkout2";
+		gpio-controller;
+		#gpio-cells = <2>;
+		extcon = <&usb2phy>;
+		wakeup-source;
+
+		charger {
+			monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+			rockchip,resistor-sense-micro-ohms = <20000>;
+			rockchip,sleep-enter-current-microamp = <300000>;
+			rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp = <100000>;
+			input-current-limit-microamp = <1600000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&pinctrl {
+	pmic {
+		pmic_int_l: pmic-int-l {
+			rockchip,pins = <0 RK_PA2 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_default>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * The OTG PHY is disabled in rk3128.dtsi, so the ACM gadget above cannot
+ * probe without this either. It is also what performs BC1.2 detection,
+ * which is the only way the charger can tell a wall adapter from a 450 mA
+ * port.
+ */
+&usb2phy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb2phy_otg {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/ {
+	/*
+	 * Every number here comes from the battery node of the vendor board
+	 * file, converted out of its hexadecimal millivolts and milliamp
+	 * hours: design_capacity 0x10af, max_chrg_current 0x578,
+	 * max_chrg_voltage 0x1068, max_input_current 0x640, bat_res 0x64,
+	 * power_off_thresd 0xd7a, sleep_enter_current 0x12c,
+	 * sleep_filter_current 0x64. The termination current is not in the
+	 * vendor DTS at all: rk816_bat_finish_ma() derives 200 mA from a pack
+	 * of 4000 mAh or more.
+	 *
+	 * The OCV table is the vendor's ocv_table read backwards, because the
+	 * vendor lists 0 % first and the power supply core wants the highest
+	 * voltage first. There is no thermistor on this board, so one table
+	 * at 20 C is all there is.
+	 */
+	battery: battery {
+		compatible = "simple-battery";
+		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <4271000>;
+		charge-term-current-microamp = <200000>;
+		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1400000>;
+		constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt = <4200000>;
+		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4200000>;
+		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3450000>;
+		factory-internal-resistance-micro-ohms = <100000>;
+		ocv-capacity-celsius = <20>;
+		ocv-capacity-table-0 = <4200000 100>, <4139000 95>,
+				       <4093000 90>, <4056000 85>,
+				       <4005000 80>, <3975000 75>,
+				       <3943000 70>, <3897000 65>,
+				       <3858000 60>, <3836000 55>,
+				       <3817000 50>, <3802000 45>,
+				       <3789000 40>, <3777000 35>,
+				       <3762000 30>, <3746000 25>,
+				       <3731000 20>, <3706000 15>,
+				       <3686000 10>, <3671000 5>,
+				       <3450000 0>;
+	};
+};
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@
 	DEFINE_RES_IRQ(RK817_IRQ_PWRON_RISE),
 };
 
+static const struct resource rk816_charger_resources[] = {
+	DEFINE_RES_IRQ(RK816_IRQ_PLUG_IN),
+	DEFINE_RES_IRQ(RK816_IRQ_PLUG_OUT),
+};
+
 static const struct resource rk817_charger_resources[] = {
 	DEFINE_RES_IRQ(RK817_IRQ_PLUG_IN),
 	DEFINE_RES_IRQ(RK817_IRQ_PLUG_OUT),
@@ -119,6 +124,11 @@
 		.num_resources = ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_rtc_resources),
 		.resources = rk816_rtc_resources,
 	},
+	{
+		.name = "rk816-charger",
+		.num_resources = ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_charger_resources),
+		.resources = rk816_charger_resources,
+	},
 };
 
 static const struct mfd_cell rk817s[] = {
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-i2c.c
@@ -99,7 +99,16 @@
 	case RK816_GGSTS_REG:
 	case RK816_ZERO_CUR_ADC_REGH:
 	case RK816_ZERO_CUR_ADC_REGL:
-	case RK816_GASCNT_REG(0) ... RK816_BAT_VOL_REGL:
+	/*
+	 * RK816_GASCNT_REG(0) is the *low* byte of the coulomb counter, so a
+	 * range starting there left the counter's three high bytes cached
+	 * along with the relax voltages and currents, the current ADC offset
+	 * calibration and the power off minute counter: under REGCACHE_MAPLE
+	 * a fuel gauge driver would read each of them once and never again.
+	 * The whole hardware updated block runs from the counter's high byte
+	 * to the sleep sample current.
+	 */
+	case RK816_GASCNT_REG(3) ... RK816_SLEEP_CON_SAMP_CUR_REG:
 		return true;
 	}
 
--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -857,6 +857,15 @@
 	  charge management and system power path management devices for single
 	  cell Li-ion and Li-polymer batteries.
 
+config CHARGER_RK816
+	tristate "Rockchip RK816 PMIC Battery Charger"
+	depends on MFD_RK8XX
+	help
+	  Say Y to include support for the Rockchip RK816 battery charger and
+	  fuel gauge. The RK816 has no hardware state of charge register, so
+	  the driver derives one from the coulomb counter and needs a
+	  monitored-battery node carrying an ocv-capacity table.
+
 config CHARGER_RK817
 	tristate "Rockchip RK817 PMIC Battery Charger"
 	depends on MFD_RK8XX
--- a/drivers/power/supply/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Makefile
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_BQ25980)	+= bq25980_charger.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_BQ25630)	+= bq25630_charger.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_BQ256XX)	+= bq256xx_charger.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_RK816)	+= rk816_charger.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_RK817)	+= rk817_charger.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_S2M)	+= s2m-charger.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_CHARGER_SGM41542)	+= sgm41542_charger.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk816_charger.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1206 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Battery and charger driver for the Rockchip RK816 PMIC.
+ *
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
+ *
+ * Shaped after drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c. Every register offset,
+ * bit position, scaling constant and default in this file was taken from the
+ * Rockchip 4.4 vendor driver (drivers/power/rk816_battery.c and
+ * rk816_battery.h) rather than from a datasheet, because that driver is what
+ * runs on the hardware this was written for.
+ *
+ * The RK816 has no hardware state-of-charge register. RK816_SOC_REG (0xe0) is
+ * the first of the battery-backed general purpose data registers - mainline
+ * already names the block RK816_DATA_REG(x) - and the vendor driver only ever
+ * writes its own computed percentage into it (rk816_bat_save_dsoc()) and reads
+ * it back on the next boot (rk816_bat_get_prev_dsoc()). It is a scratch byte,
+ * not a gauge.
+ *
+ * The real gauge is the 32 bit coulomb counter at RK816_GASCNT_REG. The vendor
+ * driver's reported percentage ("dsoc") is about 1500 lines of smoothing,
+ * zero-point bending and relearning laid over that counter's raw quotient
+ * ("rsoc"). This driver reports the quotient:
+ *
+ *   - the counter is preloaded once at probe from the relaxed open circuit
+ *     voltage looked up in the battery's ocv-capacity table, or from the
+ *     percentage the previous boot saved,
+ *   - every poll divides it by the full charge capacity,
+ *   - it is re-anchored in exactly one place, when the charger reports
+ *     termination, which is the only moment the true charge is known.
+ *
+ * Nothing is ever derived from the loaded terminal voltage, which is what
+ * keeps the percentage from swinging when a GPU load steps.
+ *
+ * What the vendor does and this driver deliberately does not do is called out
+ * at each site below: the zero algorithm, FCC relearning, current ADC offset
+ * self-calibration, and sleep discharge estimation.
+ */
+
+#include <linux/bitfield.h>
+#include <linux/bits.h>
+#include <linux/devm-helpers.h>
+#include <linux/extcon.h>
+#include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/mfd/rk808.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/power_supply.h>
+#include <linux/regmap.h>
+#include <linux/unaligned.h>
+#include <linux/workqueue.h>
+
+/* RK816_SUP_STS_REG (0xa0) */
+#define RK816_BAT_EXS			BIT(7)
+#define RK816_CHRG_STATUS_MSK		GENMASK(6, 4)
+#define RK816_USB_VLIMIT_EN		BIT(3)
+#define RK816_USB_CLIMIT_EN		BIT(2)
+
+/* RK808_VB_MON_REG (0x21), shared with the RK808 */
+#define RK816_PLUG_IN_STS		BIT(6)
+
+/* RK816_USB_CTRL_REG (0xa1) */
+#define RK816_USB_CHRG_CT_EN		BIT(7)
+#define RK816_USB_INPUT_CUR_MSK		GENMASK(3, 0)
+
+/* RK816_CHRG_CTRL(0) (0xa3) */
+#define RK816_CHRG_EN			BIT(7)
+#define RK816_CHRG_VOL_SEL_MSK		GENMASK(6, 4)
+#define RK816_CHRG_CUR_SEL_MSK		GENMASK(3, 0)
+
+/* RK816_CHRG_CTRL(1) (0xa4) */
+#define RK816_CHRG_FINISH_CUR_MSK	GENMASK(7, 6)
+
+/* RK816_CHRG_CTRL(2) (0xa5) */
+#define RK816_CHRG_TERM_DIG_SIGNAL	BIT(5)
+#define RK816_CHRG_TIMER_CCCV_EN	BIT(2)
+
+/* RK816_BAT_CTRL_REG (0xa6) */
+#define RK816_USB_SYS_EN		BIT(6)
+
+/* RK816_TS_CTRL_REG (0xac) */
+#define RK816_GG_EN			BIT(7)
+#define RK816_ADC_CUR_EN		BIT(6)
+
+/* RK816_GGCON_REG (0xb0) */
+#define RK816_ADC_CAL_MIN_MSK		GENMASK(5, 4)
+#define RK816_ADC_CAL_8MIN		0
+#define RK816_OCV_SAMP_MIN_MSK		GENMASK(3, 2)
+#define RK816_OCV_SAMP_8MIN		0
+#define RK816_ADC_CUR_MODE		BIT(1)
+
+/* RK816_GGSTS_REG (0xb1) */
+#define RK816_BAT_CON			BIT(4)
+#define RK816_RELAX_VOL12_UPD_MSK	GENMASK(3, 2)
+
+/*
+ * Battery-backed scratch registers. The PMIC is powered from the pack, so
+ * these survive a reboot and a power off but not a pack change. Software is
+ * the only thing that ever writes them; the names are the vendor's.
+ */
+#define RK816_SOC_REG			RK816_DATA_REG(0)	/* 0xe0 */
+#define RK816_REMAIN_CAP_REG(x)		RK816_DATA_REG(4 - (x))	/* 0xe1..0xe4 */
+#define RK816_NEW_FCC_REG(x)		RK816_DATA_REG(9 - (x))	/* 0xe6..0xe9 */
+#define RK816_OFF_CNT_SAVE_REG		RK816_DATA_REG(10)	/* 0xea */
+
+/* Charge state machine, RK816_SUP_STS_REG bits 6:4. */
+enum rk816_charge_status {
+	CHRG_OFF,
+	DEAD_CHRG,
+	TRICKLE_CHRG,
+	CC_OR_CV_CHRG,
+	CHARGE_FINISH,
+	USB_OVER_VOL,
+	BAT_TMP_ERR,
+	BAT_TIM_ERR,
+};
+
+/*
+ * Charge voltage, charge current and input current limit tables indexed by the
+ * register field value, copied from the vendor's CHRG_VOL_SEL[],
+ * CHRG_CUR_SEL[] and CHRG_CUR_INPUT[]. The 2250 mA step and the 80 mA input
+ * limit at index 1 are the vendor's values, not typos. The current tables hold
+ * for a 20 mOhm sense resistor.
+ */
+static const u16 rk816_chrg_vol_mv[] = {
+	4050, 4100, 4150, 4200, 4250, 4300, 4350,
+};
+
+static const u16 rk816_chrg_cur_ma[] = {
+	1000, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800, 2000, 2250, 2400,
+};
+
+static const u16 rk816_input_cur_ma[] = {
+	450, 80, 850, 1000, 1250, 1500, 1750, 2000,
+};
+
+/*
+ * The ADC scaling constants hold for a 20 mOhm sense resistor: one current LSB
+ * is 1506 uA and one coulomb count is 1/2390 mAh. res_div is 2 for 20 mOhm and
+ * 1 for 10 mOhm, so halving the resistor doubles what each LSB is worth. That
+ * reproduces the vendor's res_fac arithmetic exactly for both values it
+ * supports on this part.
+ */
+#define RK816_ADC_TO_CURRENT(adc, res_div)	((adc) * 1506 * 2 / (res_div))
+#define RK816_UA_PER_LSB(res_div)		RK816_ADC_TO_CURRENT(1, res_div)
+#define RK816_ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH(adc, res_div)	\
+	div_s64((s64)(adc) * 200, 239 * (res_div))
+#define RK816_CHARGE_TO_ADC(uah, res_div)	\
+	div_s64((s64)(uah) * 239 * (res_div), 200)
+
+/* rk817-charger polls every 8 s; the vendor's monitor_sec default is 5. */
+#define RK816_MONITOR_MS		8000
+
+/*
+ * The vendor treats a saved charge as worthless once the PMIC has been off for
+ * half an hour (is_rk816_bat_ocv_valid()): the counter does not run while the
+ * gauge is unpowered, and a pack left alone that long has relaxed enough for
+ * the OCV to be honest instead.
+ */
+#define RK816_OFF_MIN_OCV_VALID		30
+
+/* The vendor's own lower sanity bound on a stored FCC, in mAh (MIN_FCC). */
+#define RK816_MIN_FCC_MAH		500
+
+struct rk816_charger {
+	struct device *dev;
+	struct regmap *regmap;
+	struct power_supply *bat_ps;
+	struct power_supply *usb_ps;
+	struct power_supply *ac_ps;
+	struct extcon_dev *edev;
+	struct notifier_block cable_nb;
+	struct delayed_work work;
+	struct delayed_work cable_work;
+	struct mutex lock;	/* serialises the register state below */
+
+	/* Board description, from the device tree. */
+	int res_div;
+	u32 sleep_enter_current_ua;
+	u32 sleep_filter_current_ua;
+	u32 input_current_limit_ua;
+	u32 charge_full_design_uah;
+	int voltage_min_design_uv;
+	int voltage_max_design_uv;
+	struct power_supply_battery_info *bat_info;
+
+	/* Voltage ADC calibration: millivolts = k * adc / 1000 + b. */
+	int voltage_k;
+	int voltage_b;
+
+	/* Live state. */
+	int fcc_uah;
+	int charge_now_uah;
+	int volt_avg_uv;
+	int cur_avg_ua;
+	int soc;
+	int charge_status;
+	bool battery_present;
+	bool plugged_in;
+	bool usb_online;
+	bool ac_online;
+};
+
+static int rk816_bat_read16be(struct rk816_charger *cg, unsigned int reg)
+{
+	u8 buf[2];
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_bulk_read(cg->regmap, reg, buf, sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	return get_unaligned_be16(buf);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The voltage ADC is calibrated in the factory at 3.0 V and 4.2 V, and the two
+ * points are burned into VCALIB0 and VCALIB1. The vendor turns them into a
+ * straight line in millivolts and then applies a fixed 1.1 divider correction
+ * on the way out; both are reproduced here exactly.
+ */
+static int rk816_bat_calib_vol(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	int vcalib0, vcalib1;
+
+	vcalib0 = rk816_bat_read16be(cg, RK816_VCALIB0_REGH);
+	if (vcalib0 < 0)
+		return vcalib0;
+
+	vcalib1 = rk816_bat_read16be(cg, RK816_VCALIB1_REGH);
+	if (vcalib1 < 0)
+		return vcalib1;
+
+	if (vcalib1 == vcalib0)
+		return dev_err_probe(cg->dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "bad voltage calibration: vcalib0 == vcalib1 == %d\n",
+				     vcalib0);
+
+	cg->voltage_k = (4200 - 3000) * 1000 / (vcalib1 - vcalib0);
+	cg->voltage_b = 4200 - (cg->voltage_k * vcalib1) / 1000;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_get_vol_uv(struct rk816_charger *cg, unsigned int reg)
+{
+	int adc = rk816_bat_read16be(cg, reg);
+
+	if (adc < 0)
+		return adc;
+
+	return (cg->voltage_k * adc / 1000 + cg->voltage_b) * 1100;
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_get_cur_ua(struct rk816_charger *cg, int *cur_ua)
+{
+	int adc = rk816_bat_read16be(cg, RK816_BAT_CUR_AVG_REGH);
+
+	if (adc < 0)
+		return adc;
+
+	/*
+	 * The average current ADC is 12 bit two's complement, positive while
+	 * charging. The vendor open codes the sign extension on the unmasked
+	 * 16 bit value ("if (val & 0x800) val -= 4096"), which is identical
+	 * for every legal reading and differs only if the high byte ever
+	 * carries something above bit 11.
+	 */
+	*cur_ua = RK816_ADC_TO_CURRENT(sign_extend32(adc, 11), cg->res_div);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_get_charge_uah(struct rk816_charger *cg, int *uah)
+{
+	u8 buf[4];
+	int ret;
+
+	/* RK816_GASCNT_REG(3) is 0xb8, the most significant byte. */
+	ret = regmap_bulk_read(cg->regmap, RK816_GASCNT_REG(3), buf,
+			       sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	*uah = RK816_ADC_TO_CHARGE_UAH((s32)get_unaligned_be32(buf),
+				       cg->res_div);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Preload the coulomb counter through its calibration register. */
+static int rk816_bat_set_charge_uah(struct rk816_charger *cg, int uah)
+{
+	u8 buf[4];
+
+	put_unaligned_be32(RK816_CHARGE_TO_ADC(uah, cg->res_div), buf);
+
+	return regmap_bulk_write(cg->regmap, RK816_GASCNT_CAL_REG(3), buf,
+				 sizeof(buf));
+}
+
+/*
+ * Mirror the percentage, the remaining capacity and the full charge capacity
+ * into the battery-backed scratch registers, in the vendor's layout and byte
+ * order, so the next boot of either kernel starts from something sane.
+ */
+static int rk816_bat_save_nvram(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	u8 buf[4];
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_write(cg->regmap, RK816_SOC_REG, cg->soc);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	put_unaligned_be32(cg->charge_now_uah / 1000, buf);
+	ret = regmap_bulk_write(cg->regmap, RK816_REMAIN_CAP_REG(3), buf,
+				sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	put_unaligned_be32(cg->fcc_uah / 1000, buf);
+
+	return regmap_bulk_write(cg->regmap, RK816_NEW_FCC_REG(3), buf,
+				 sizeof(buf));
+}
+
+/* Called with cg->lock held. */
+static void rk816_bat_read_props(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	unsigned int reg;
+	int ret, val;
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_get_vol_uv(cg, RK816_BAT_VOL_REGH);
+	if (ret >= 0)
+		cg->volt_avg_uv = ret;
+
+	if (!rk816_bat_get_cur_ua(cg, &val))
+		cg->cur_avg_ua = val;
+
+	if (!regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK816_SUP_STS_REG, &reg)) {
+		cg->battery_present = reg & RK816_BAT_EXS;
+		cg->charge_status = FIELD_GET(RK816_CHRG_STATUS_MSK, reg);
+	}
+
+	if (!regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK808_VB_MON_REG, &reg))
+		cg->plugged_in = reg & RK816_PLUG_IN_STS;
+
+	/*
+	 * The PMIC knows VBUS is there but not what is supplying it, and the
+	 * USB_EXIST/USB_EFF bits in SUP_STS are dead code in the vendor driver
+	 * (their only uses are unreachable case labels in a switch on bits
+	 * 6:4). So presence is PLUG_IN_STS, and BC1.2 through extcon only ever
+	 * refines it. This is the vendor's rk816_bat_check_charger(), which
+	 * overrides extcon in both directions for the same reason.
+	 */
+	if (cg->plugged_in && !cg->usb_online && !cg->ac_online)
+		cg->usb_online = true;
+	else if (!cg->plugged_in)
+		cg->usb_online = cg->ac_online = false;
+
+	if (rk816_bat_get_charge_uah(cg, &val))
+		return;
+
+	/*
+	 * Charge termination is the one moment the true charge is known, so
+	 * the counter is re-anchored here and nowhere else. The correction is
+	 * always upward and always at 100 %, but it is a visible step if the
+	 * counter had drifted low.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor additionally relearns the full charge capacity from the
+	 * charge accumulated between a low starting point and this moment
+	 * (rk816_bat_update_age_algorithm()). That is not done here: an aged
+	 * pack will read optimistically, and it will do so silently.
+	 */
+	if (cg->charge_status == CHARGE_FINISH && val < cg->fcc_uah) {
+		rk816_bat_set_charge_uah(cg, cg->fcc_uah);
+		val = cg->fcc_uah;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The percentage is the raw quotient, the vendor's "rsoc". There is
+	 * deliberately no zero algorithm: the vendor bends the last few
+	 * percent so that 0 % lands on the power-off voltage under real load
+	 * (rk816_bat_zero_algorithm()), which means this driver can report a
+	 * few percent left when the pack hits its cut-off, and can report 0 %
+	 * with charge to spare. Shut the system down on voltage, not on this.
+	 */
+	cg->charge_now_uah = clamp(val, 0, cg->fcc_uah);
+	cg->soc = clamp(cg->charge_now_uah / (cg->fcc_uah / 100), 0, 100);
+
+	rk816_bat_save_nvram(cg);
+}
+
+static void rk816_charging_monitor(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = container_of(work, struct rk816_charger,
+						work.work);
+	int old_soc, old_status;
+	bool old_usb, old_ac;
+
+	mutex_lock(&cg->lock);
+	old_soc = cg->soc;
+	old_status = cg->charge_status;
+	old_usb = cg->usb_online;
+	old_ac = cg->ac_online;
+	rk816_bat_read_props(cg);
+	mutex_unlock(&cg->lock);
+
+	if (cg->soc != old_soc || cg->charge_status != old_status)
+		power_supply_changed(cg->bat_ps);
+	if (cg->usb_online != old_usb)
+		power_supply_changed(cg->usb_ps);
+	if (cg->ac_online != old_ac)
+		power_supply_changed(cg->ac_ps);
+
+	queue_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &cg->work,
+			   msecs_to_jiffies(RK816_MONITOR_MS));
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_get_prop(struct power_supply *ps,
+			      enum power_supply_property prop,
+			      union power_supply_propval *val)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = power_supply_get_drvdata(ps);
+
+	switch (prop) {
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
+		val->intval = cg->battery_present;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
+		if (!cg->usb_online && !cg->ac_online) {
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
+			break;
+		}
+		switch (cg->charge_status) {
+		case CHRG_OFF:
+		case USB_OVER_VOL:
+		case BAT_TMP_ERR:
+		case BAT_TIM_ERR:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
+			break;
+		case CHARGE_FINISH:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
+			break;
+		default:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			break;
+		}
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_TYPE:
+		switch (cg->charge_status) {
+		case DEAD_CHRG:
+		case TRICKLE_CHRG:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_TRICKLE;
+			break;
+		case CC_OR_CV_CHRG:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_STANDARD;
+			break;
+		default:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_NONE;
+			break;
+		}
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_HEALTH:
+		switch (cg->charge_status) {
+		case BAT_TMP_ERR:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_OVERHEAT;
+			break;
+		case USB_OVER_VOL:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_OVERVOLTAGE;
+			break;
+		case BAT_TIM_ERR:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_SAFETY_TIMER_EXPIRE;
+			break;
+		default:
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_GOOD;
+			break;
+		}
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY:
+		val->intval = cg->soc;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW:
+		val->intval = cg->charge_now_uah;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL:
+		val->intval = cg->fcc_uah;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
+		val->intval = cg->charge_full_design_uah;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_AVG:
+		val->intval = cg->volt_avg_uv;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_AVG:
+		val->intval = cg->cur_avg_ua;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MIN_DESIGN:
+		val->intval = cg->voltage_min_design_uv;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MAX_DESIGN:
+		val->intval = cg->voltage_max_design_uv;
+		break;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY:
+		val->intval = cg->bat_info->technology;
+		break;
+	default:
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_usb_get_prop(struct power_supply *ps,
+			      enum power_supply_property prop,
+			      union power_supply_propval *val)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = power_supply_get_drvdata(ps);
+
+	switch (prop) {
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE:
+		val->intval = cg->usb_online;
+		break;
+	default:
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_ac_get_prop(struct power_supply *ps,
+			     enum power_supply_property prop,
+			     union power_supply_propval *val)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = power_supply_get_drvdata(ps);
+
+	switch (prop) {
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE:
+		val->intval = cg->ac_online;
+		break;
+	default:
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const enum power_supply_property rk816_bat_props[] = {
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_TYPE,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_HEALTH,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_AVG,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_AVG,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MIN_DESIGN,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MAX_DESIGN,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY,
+};
+
+static const enum power_supply_property rk816_online_props[] = {
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE,
+};
+
+/*
+ * "battery", "usb" and "ac" rather than rk817-charger's "rk817-battery" and
+ * "rk817-charger": on this class of board those three names under
+ * /sys/class/power_supply are the userspace ABI.
+ */
+static const struct power_supply_desc rk816_bat_desc = {
+	.name = "battery",
+	.type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_BATTERY,
+	.properties = rk816_bat_props,
+	.num_properties = ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_bat_props),
+	.get_property = rk816_bat_get_prop,
+};
+
+static const struct power_supply_desc rk816_usb_desc = {
+	.name = "usb",
+	.type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_USB,
+	.properties = rk816_online_props,
+	.num_properties = ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_online_props),
+	.get_property = rk816_usb_get_prop,
+};
+
+static const struct power_supply_desc rk816_ac_desc = {
+	.name = "ac",
+	.type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_MAINS,
+	.properties = rk816_online_props,
+	.num_properties = ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_online_props),
+	.get_property = rk816_ac_get_prop,
+};
+
+static irqreturn_t rk816_plug_isr(int irq, void *data)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = data;
+
+	mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &cg->work, 0);
+
+	return IRQ_HANDLED;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Program the input current limit. The selection walk is the vendor's
+ * rk816_bat_select_chrg_cv(): index 1 is 80 mA and is only ever chosen for a
+ * request of 80 mA or less, anything below 850 mA takes index 0 (450 mA), and
+ * everything above that walks the table from index 2 downwards to the largest
+ * entry that does not exceed the request.
+ */
+static int rk816_bat_set_input_current(struct rk816_charger *cg, u32 limit_ua)
+{
+	unsigned int limit_ma = limit_ua / 1000;
+	unsigned int i, sel;
+
+	if (limit_ma <= 80) {
+		sel = 1;
+	} else if (limit_ma < 850) {
+		sel = 0;
+	} else {
+		sel = 2;
+		for (i = 2; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_input_cur_ma); i++) {
+			if (limit_ma < rk816_input_cur_ma[i])
+				break;
+			sel = i;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_USB_CTRL_REG,
+				  RK816_USB_INPUT_CUR_MSK,
+				  FIELD_PREP(RK816_USB_INPUT_CUR_MSK, sel));
+}
+
+static void rk816_bat_update_cables(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	bool sdp, dcp, cdp;
+	u32 limit_ua;
+
+	sdp = extcon_get_state(cg->edev, EXTCON_CHG_USB_SDP) > 0;
+	dcp = extcon_get_state(cg->edev, EXTCON_CHG_USB_DCP) > 0;
+	cdp = extcon_get_state(cg->edev, EXTCON_CHG_USB_CDP) > 0;
+
+	mutex_lock(&cg->lock);
+	cg->ac_online = dcp;
+	cg->usb_online = sdp || cdp;
+
+	if (dcp)
+		limit_ua = cg->input_current_limit_ua;
+	else if (cdp)
+		limit_ua = 1500000;
+	else
+		limit_ua = 450000;
+
+	rk816_bat_set_input_current(cg, limit_ua);
+	mutex_unlock(&cg->lock);
+
+	power_supply_changed(cg->usb_ps);
+	power_supply_changed(cg->ac_ps);
+}
+
+static void rk816_extcon_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = container_of(work, struct rk816_charger,
+						cable_work.work);
+
+	rk816_bat_update_cables(cg);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The extcon notifier chain can run in a context that must not sleep, and
+ * every reaction to it is an i2c transfer, so push the work out to a
+ * workqueue. The vendor driver does the same for the same reason.
+ */
+static int rk816_cable_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
+				unsigned long event, void *ptr)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = container_of(nb, struct rk816_charger,
+						cable_nb);
+
+	mod_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &cg->cable_work, 0);
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_init_charger(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	struct power_supply_battery_info *info = cg->bat_info;
+	unsigned int chrg_vol_mv, chrg_cur_ma, finish_ma, i;
+	unsigned int vol_sel = 0, cur_sel = 0, finish_sel;
+	int ret;
+
+	chrg_vol_mv = info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv / 1000;
+	chrg_cur_ma = info->constant_charge_current_max_ua / 1000;
+	finish_ma = info->charge_term_current_ua / 1000;
+
+	if (chrg_vol_mv < rk816_chrg_vol_mv[0])
+		return dev_err_probe(cg->dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "constant-charge-voltage-max %u mV below the lowest the RK816 can select\n",
+				     chrg_vol_mv);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_chrg_vol_mv); i++) {
+		if (chrg_vol_mv < rk816_chrg_vol_mv[i])
+			break;
+		vol_sel = i;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The charge current table holds for 20 mOhm. With 10 mOhm the same
+	 * register value delivers twice the current, so halve the request
+	 * before the lookup, which is what the vendor's res_fac division does.
+	 */
+	if (cg->res_div == 1)
+		chrg_cur_ma /= 2;
+
+	if (chrg_cur_ma < rk816_chrg_cur_ma[0])
+		return dev_err_probe(cg->dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "constant-charge-current-max %u mA below the lowest the RK816 can select\n",
+				     chrg_cur_ma);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rk816_chrg_cur_ma); i++) {
+		if (chrg_cur_ma < rk816_chrg_cur_ma[i])
+			break;
+		cur_sel = i;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Termination current: 100, 150, 200 or 250 mA at 20 mOhm, halved
+	 * again for 10 mOhm. The vendor never reads this from the device tree
+	 * at all; rk816_bat_finish_ma() picks 200 mA for any pack of 4000 mAh
+	 * or more, which is what charge-term-current-microamp carries here.
+	 */
+	if (cg->res_div == 1)
+		finish_ma /= 2;
+	finish_sel = clamp(finish_ma / 50, 2U, 5U) - 2;
+
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_CHRG_CTRL(0),
+				 RK816_CHRG_EN | RK816_CHRG_VOL_SEL_MSK |
+				 RK816_CHRG_CUR_SEL_MSK,
+				 RK816_CHRG_EN |
+				 FIELD_PREP(RK816_CHRG_VOL_SEL_MSK, vol_sel) |
+				 FIELD_PREP(RK816_CHRG_CUR_SEL_MSK, cur_sel));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_CHRG_CTRL(1),
+				 RK816_CHRG_FINISH_CUR_MSK,
+				 FIELD_PREP(RK816_CHRG_FINISH_CUR_MSK,
+					    finish_sel));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Digital termination, and the CC/CV safety timer off: the vendor
+	 * clears CHRG_TIMER_CCCV_EN because on a large pack the timer expires
+	 * mid charge, reports TIMER_ERR and stops charging a healthy battery.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_CHRG_CTRL(2),
+				 RK816_CHRG_TERM_DIG_SIGNAL |
+				 RK816_CHRG_TIMER_CCCV_EN,
+				 RK816_CHRG_TERM_DIG_SIGNAL);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Input voltage and input current limiters on. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_SUP_STS_REG,
+				 RK816_USB_VLIMIT_EN | RK816_USB_CLIMIT_EN,
+				 RK816_USB_VLIMIT_EN | RK816_USB_CLIMIT_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Route the charger input to the system rail. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_BAT_CTRL_REG,
+				 RK816_USB_SYS_EN, RK816_USB_SYS_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Charge current thermal feedback off: it is the vendor's fb_temp
+	 * option, which defaults off, and there is no thermistor here.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_USB_CTRL_REG,
+				 RK816_USB_CHRG_CT_EN, 0);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Until something says otherwise, assume a 450 mA port. */
+	return rk816_bat_set_input_current(cg, 450000);
+}
+
+static int rk816_bat_init_gauge(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	u8 buf[2];
+	int ret, thres;
+
+	/* Gauge and current ADC on. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_TS_CTRL_REG,
+				 RK816_GG_EN | RK816_ADC_CUR_EN,
+				 RK816_GG_EN | RK816_ADC_CUR_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Average current mode, ADC offset calibration every 8 minutes, OCV
+	 * sampled every 8 minutes. These are the vendor's
+	 * rk816_bat_init_chrg_config() values.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor additionally re-zeroes the current ADC in software when
+	 * it sees a relaxed pack (rk816_bat_init_coffset()). That is not done
+	 * here, so a small systematic current error accumulates into the
+	 * counter between full charges.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_GGCON_REG,
+				 RK816_ADC_CAL_MIN_MSK |
+				 RK816_OCV_SAMP_MIN_MSK |
+				 RK816_ADC_CUR_MODE,
+				 RK816_ADC_CAL_8MIN | RK816_OCV_SAMP_8MIN |
+				 RK816_ADC_CUR_MODE);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Relax entry and exit thresholds, in current ADC counts. The vendor
+	 * uses sleep_enter_current for the entry and sleep_exit_current for
+	 * the exit; every board it ships sets them to the same value, and this
+	 * board's device tree does too, so one property covers both.
+	 */
+	thres = cg->sleep_enter_current_ua / RK816_UA_PER_LSB(cg->res_div);
+	put_unaligned_be16(thres, buf);
+	ret = regmap_bulk_write(cg->regmap, RK816_RELAX_ENTRY_THRES_REGH,
+				buf, sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_bulk_write(cg->regmap, RK816_RELAX_EXIT_THRES_REGH,
+				buf, sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The sleep sample current threshold is scaled for 20 mOhm whatever
+	 * the sense resistor is; the vendor does not correct this one either.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_write(cg->regmap, RK816_SLEEP_CON_SAMP_CUR_REG,
+			   cg->sleep_filter_current_ua / 1506);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Restart relax voltage sampling so the next OCV is fresh. */
+	return regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_GGSTS_REG,
+				  RK816_RELAX_VOL12_UPD_MSK, 0);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Minutes the PMIC spent powered off, the vendor's
+ * rk816_bat_get_pwroff_min(): the hardware counts in
+ * RK816_NON_ACT_TIMER_CNT_REG and software keeps the previous reading in a
+ * scratch byte, so a count that has not moved means we did not go through a
+ * power off at all.
+ */
+static int rk816_bat_off_minutes(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	unsigned int now_min, last_min;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK816_NON_ACT_TIMER_CNT_REG, &now_min);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK816_OFF_CNT_SAVE_REG, &last_min);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_write(cg->regmap, RK816_OFF_CNT_SAVE_REG, now_min);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	return (now_min != last_min) ? now_min : 0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Decide what the charge is at probe and preload the coulomb counter with it.
+ * The three cases are the vendor's three cases:
+ *
+ *  - BAT_CON set: the pack was just connected and nothing carried over, so
+ *    look the relaxed OCV up in the ocv-capacity table,
+ *  - the PMIC was off for RK816_OFF_MIN_OCV_VALID minutes or more: the counter
+ *    did not run while it was unpowered, so throw the saved value away and use
+ *    the OCV, which that long a rest has made honest,
+ *  - anything else: trust the percentage the last boot saved.
+ */
+static int rk816_bat_init_soc(struct rk816_charger *cg)
+{
+	unsigned int reg, saved_soc;
+	bool first_boot;
+	u8 buf[4];
+	u32 fcc_mah;
+	int ret, off_min, ocv_uv, ocv_soc;
+
+	ret = regmap_bulk_read(cg->regmap, RK816_NEW_FCC_REG(3), buf,
+			       sizeof(buf));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	fcc_mah = get_unaligned_be32(buf);
+
+	/*
+	 * The vendor's sanity window on a stored FCC, except that the upper
+	 * bound is the design capacity rather than design_qmax: nothing here
+	 * relearns the capacity, so a stored value above the design capacity
+	 * can only be garbage or a vendor kernel's relearned value, and taking
+	 * the conservative one of the two is the safe way to be wrong.
+	 */
+	if (fcc_mah < RK816_MIN_FCC_MAH ||
+	    fcc_mah > cg->charge_full_design_uah / 1000)
+		fcc_mah = cg->charge_full_design_uah / 1000;
+	cg->fcc_uah = fcc_mah * 1000;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK816_GGSTS_REG, &reg);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	first_boot = reg & RK816_BAT_CON;
+
+	off_min = rk816_bat_off_minutes(cg);
+	if (off_min < 0)
+		return off_min;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(cg->regmap, RK816_SOC_REG, &saved_soc);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (first_boot || off_min >= RK816_OFF_MIN_OCV_VALID ||
+	    saved_soc > 100) {
+		ocv_uv = rk816_bat_get_vol_uv(cg, RK816_BAT_OCV_REGH);
+		if (ocv_uv < 0)
+			return ocv_uv;
+
+		/*
+		 * No thermistor is fitted on this board, so ask the table for
+		 * 20 degrees, the same assumption rk817-charger makes.
+		 */
+		ocv_soc = power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap(cg->bat_info, ocv_uv,
+						       20);
+		if (ocv_soc < 0)
+			return dev_err_probe(cg->dev, ocv_soc,
+					     "no usable ocv-capacity table\n");
+
+		cg->soc = clamp(ocv_soc, 0, 100);
+		dev_info(cg->dev,
+			 "seeded %d%% from ocv %d uV (first boot %d, off %d min)\n",
+			 cg->soc, ocv_uv, first_boot, off_min);
+
+		if (first_boot) {
+			ret = regmap_update_bits(cg->regmap, RK816_GGSTS_REG,
+						 RK816_BAT_CON, 0);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+	} else {
+		cg->soc = saved_soc;
+		dev_info(cg->dev, "restored %d%% from the last boot\n",
+			 cg->soc);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * There is also no correction for what the pack lost in suspend: the
+	 * counter keeps counting while the SoC is down, but the vendor's sleep
+	 * discharge estimate (rk816_bat_calc_sleep_dischrg()) that catches
+	 * what the gauge misses is not reproduced here.
+	 */
+	cg->charge_now_uah = cg->soc * (cg->fcc_uah / 100);
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_set_charge_uah(cg, cg->charge_now_uah);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	return rk816_bat_save_nvram(cg);
+}
+
+static void rk816_bat_put_info(void *data)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = data;
+
+	power_supply_put_battery_info(cg->bat_ps, cg->bat_info);
+}
+
+static void rk816_cleanup_node(void *data)
+{
+	of_node_put(data);
+}
+
+static int rk816_charger_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct rk808 *rk808 = dev_get_drvdata(pdev->dev.parent);
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct power_supply_config pscfg = {};
+	struct rk816_charger *cg;
+	struct device_node *node;
+	int ret, irq;
+	u32 of_value;
+
+	node = of_get_child_by_name(dev->parent->of_node, "charger");
+	if (!node)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, rk816_cleanup_node, node);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	cg = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*cg), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!cg)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	cg->dev = dev;
+	cg->regmap = rk808->regmap;
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, cg);
+
+	ret = devm_mutex_init(dev, &cg->lock);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "rockchip,resistor-sense-micro-ohms",
+				   &of_value);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "missing rockchip,resistor-sense-micro-ohms\n");
+	if (of_value != 10000 && of_value != 20000)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "unsupported sense resistor %u uOhm\n",
+				     of_value);
+	cg->res_div = (of_value == 20000) ? 2 : 1;
+
+	ret = of_property_read_u32(node,
+				   "rockchip,sleep-enter-current-microamp",
+				   &cg->sleep_enter_current_ua);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "missing rockchip,sleep-enter-current-microamp\n");
+
+	ret = of_property_read_u32(node,
+				   "rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp",
+				   &cg->sleep_filter_current_ua);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "missing rockchip,sleep-filter-current-microamp\n");
+
+	cg->input_current_limit_ua = 450000;
+	of_property_read_u32(node, "input-current-limit-microamp",
+			     &cg->input_current_limit_ua);
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_calib_vol(cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	pscfg.drv_data = cg;
+	pscfg.fwnode = &node->fwnode;
+
+	cg->bat_ps = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &rk816_bat_desc, &pscfg);
+	if (IS_ERR(cg->bat_ps))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cg->bat_ps),
+				     "failed to register battery\n");
+
+	cg->usb_ps = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &rk816_usb_desc, &pscfg);
+	if (IS_ERR(cg->usb_ps))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cg->usb_ps),
+				     "failed to register usb supply\n");
+
+	cg->ac_ps = devm_power_supply_register(dev, &rk816_ac_desc, &pscfg);
+	if (IS_ERR(cg->ac_ps))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cg->ac_ps),
+				     "failed to register ac supply\n");
+
+	ret = power_supply_get_battery_info(cg->bat_ps, &cg->bat_info);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "unable to get battery info\n");
+
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, rk816_bat_put_info, cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (cg->bat_info->charge_full_design_uah <= 0 ||
+	    cg->bat_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua <= 0 ||
+	    cg->bat_info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv <= 0 ||
+	    cg->bat_info->charge_term_current_ua <= 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
+				     "monitored-battery is missing a required value\n");
+
+	cg->charge_full_design_uah = cg->bat_info->charge_full_design_uah;
+	cg->voltage_min_design_uv = cg->bat_info->voltage_min_design_uv;
+	cg->voltage_max_design_uv = cg->bat_info->voltage_max_design_uv;
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_init_gauge(cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to init the fuel gauge\n");
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_init_charger(cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to init the charger\n");
+
+	ret = rk816_bat_init_soc(cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to init the state of charge\n");
+
+	ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &cg->work,
+					   rk816_charging_monitor);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Resource 0 is PLUG_IN and resource 1 PLUG_OUT, per the MFD cell. */
+	irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
+	if (irq < 0)
+		return irq;
+	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, irq, NULL, rk816_plug_isr,
+					IRQF_ONESHOT, "rk816-plug-in", cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to request the plug in irq\n");
+
+	irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 1);
+	if (irq < 0)
+		return irq;
+	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, irq, NULL, rk816_plug_isr,
+					IRQF_ONESHOT, "rk816-plug-out", cg);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to request the plug out irq\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * The PMIC can tell that VBUS is present but not what is on the other
+	 * end of it, so when the SoC's USB PHY does BC1.2 detection take SDP,
+	 * CDP and DCP from there. Without it every charger is a 450 mA port
+	 * and "ac" is permanently offline: slow, but not a lie.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_present(dev->parent->of_node, "extcon")) {
+		ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &cg->cable_work,
+						   rk816_extcon_work);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		cg->edev = extcon_get_edev_by_phandle(dev->parent, 0);
+		if (IS_ERR(cg->edev))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cg->edev),
+					     "invalid extcon\n");
+
+		cg->cable_nb.notifier_call = rk816_cable_notifier;
+		ret = devm_extcon_register_notifier_all(dev, cg->edev,
+							&cg->cable_nb);
+		if (ret)
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+					     "failed to register the extcon notifier\n");
+
+		rk816_bat_update_cables(cg);
+	}
+
+	queue_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &cg->work, 0);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_charger_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&cg->work);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int rk816_charger_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct rk816_charger *cg = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/*
+	 * Poll immediately: the counter kept counting through suspend but
+	 * nothing was published, so the first value userspace reads after a
+	 * resume should be a fresh one.
+	 */
+	queue_delayed_work(system_percpu_wq, &cg->work, 0);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rk816_charger_pm, rk816_charger_suspend,
+				rk816_charger_resume);
+
+static struct platform_driver rk816_charger_driver = {
+	.probe = rk816_charger_probe,
+	.driver = {
+		.name = "rk816-charger",
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&rk816_charger_pm),
+	},
+};
+module_platform_driver(rk816_charger_driver);
+
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Battery and charger driver for the Rockchip RK816 PMIC");
+MODULE_AUTHOR("Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>");
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+MODULE_ALIAS("platform:rk816-charger");
